    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\sin3\\theta=3\\sin\\theta-4\\sin^3\\theta$.\n\nExpand $\\sin(2\\theta+\\theta)$ and substitute the double-angle identities.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sin3\\theta&=\\sin(2\\theta+\\theta)\\\\\\sin3\\theta&=\\sin2\\theta\\cos\\theta+\\cos2\\theta\\sin\\theta\\\\\\sin3\\theta&=2\\sin\\theta\\cos^2\\theta+(1-2\\sin^2\\theta)\\sin\\theta\\\\\\sin3\\theta&=2\\sin\\theta(1-\\sin^2\\theta)+\\sin\\theta-2\\sin^3\\theta\\\\\\sin3\\theta&=3\\sin\\theta-4\\sin^3\\theta\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 44
